/-!
# Rank-one configuration for the characteristic-two exclusion

The minimal-outside argument proves `I = LS` and uniqueness of `M ∩ I`
once `Y₊ ≤ L` is established. The conjugate-pair criterion proves the
internal product from the unique-central-involution geometry with relative
normality in the local overgroup.

The source assembly of 15.3.27–32 remains open: component normality and
containment, the precise parabolic alternatives and their exclusions,
the compatible `S₈` module, and the residual-centralizer calculations
must still be constructed. None is supplied by the conditional reductions.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004),
printed pp.1130–1133.
-/
